# The last pattern that matches a file decides its owners. The ruleset of main requires a code owner's approval of
# each change to an owned file.
# Under .github/, a code owner only where a change can reach a credential or decide a required check
# (dispatch://INFRA-5359/spec#b-r10): one line for each file of the inventory that .github/scripts/workflow-credentials
# prints, and no line for a directory there, so a file added under .github/ has no owner until a line names it. The
# exception is an agent instruction or skill (AGENTS*.md, CLAUDE*.md, SKILL.md, a file under skills/ or .claude/),
# which the patterns for the whole repository own at any depth; such a file under .github/ is no file of the inventory,
# so workflow-credentials fails a pull request that adds one there. That script, which the required check tests runs,
# fails when a file of the inventory has no owner here or another file under .github/ has one. It reads what the jobs
# of these workflows run or read in a small set of forms (SUPPORTED, in that script), and fails on any other form that
# it cannot resolve; a path that a job assembles from parts is the one thing it does not see, and the code owner's
# review of the owned file that assembles it covers it. This holds while main's ruleset requires the four required
# checks from the oss-verify App (5447700), as theorem-labs/agent-infra#7010 made it, so a job of a workflow with no
# owner cannot post one.
# Files with no owner on purpose: the files that no pattern matches (most files of src/, tests/, docs/ and projects/,
# and the files under .github/ that are no file of the inventory).
